/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-18T17:31:53-07:00","id":1131027,"title":"","content":"Aside from sample antagonists, I wonder what else it contains (rules updates for pure gifts and Bale Hounds are probably included.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-18T17:34:12-07:00","id":1131028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The young man in the cafe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1131020-night-horrors-shunned-by-the-moon?p=1131027#post1131027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aside from sample antagonists, I wonder what else it contains (rules updates for pure gifts and Bale Hounds are probably included.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't be surprised if the rules for creating the Pure from DEC got reprinted. Ghost Wolf specific gifts would be pretty cool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-18T17:41:03-07:00","id":1131032,"title":"","content":"This poor, maligned, abandoned gameline! Those evil devs starving it of content!<br /> <br /> I kid, I kid. Very surprised and excited to see Ghost Wolves rolled up in this; I've always liked them more than the Tribes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-18T17:56:19-07:00","id":1131039,"title":"","content":"Yay! If it's got rules for them all, the way that the strix and Dampier and such were covered in the vampire night horrors book, this is perfect. Not only is it good to see updates, but Bale Hounds and the Pure being in one book makes it so convenient. On top of that, the only werewolves in my game are ghost wolves and ivory claws.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-18T18:41:44-07:00","id":1131053,"title":"","content":"So, it's just the black shee--er, black <i>wolves</i> then? Cool, it's good to get those bases covered. I'd like to see a Predators update too, or a Shadow deep-dive, but I suppose a book a year is all I can afford to keep up with...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-18T18:57:46-07:00","id":1131060,"title":"","content":"I know Blood Talons are going to be looking forward to it!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-18T18:58:03-07:00","id":1131061,"title":"","content":"I'd love to see spirits covered with a book someday, but they're considerably easier to update than Hosts and these moon shunned (in fact, just having one word to describe the whole lot is already a nice organic step forward). Spirit numina may need some updates, but that's far less of an undertaking than moon shunned.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-18T19:09:08-07:00","id":1131063,"title":"","content":"Pure <i>and </i>Bale Hounds in a single book, also covering Ghost Wolves? Very nice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-18T19:16:19-07:00","id":1131066,"title":"","content":"Secrets of the Tribes will also be a thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-18T19:31:17-07:00","id":1131078,"title":"","content":"Finally some good news. Really nice to hear this.<br /> <br /> Apparently our developer bowed out a while back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 08-18-2017, 10:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-18T19:43:33-07:00","id":1131086,"title":"","content":"Oh, he did? I figured it was a huge workload with two gamelines and the Apocalypse having like 20+ books or something coming along. Any idea who the new person is?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-18T19:48:31-07:00","id":1131087,"title":"","content":"No word on a new developer. That'd be nice, especially since nothing seems to go forward without one.<br /> <br /> Apparently doing two gamelines was a part of it but also his real job had a lot more duties to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 08-18-2017, 11:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-18T21:32:45-07:00","id":1131115,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1131020-night-horrors-shunned-by-the-moon?p=1131078#post1131078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Finally some good news. Really nice to hear this.<br /> <br /> Apparently our developer bowed out a while back.</div> </div> </div> </div>Called it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-18T21:34:10-07:00","id":1131116,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure how I feel about getting a Night Horrors book that's focused, primarily, on other werewolves, but the Pure and Bale Hounds need some love. The update to the Pure in Forsaken By Rome was very nice, but it doesn't give them any new Shadow Gifts or Wolf Gifts, which would have been interesting to see. Also, if we get Bale Hounds updated, we might get to see what an Infernal/Lower Depths Ephemeral Being looks like, even if it's just a template the way Abyssal Being is now.<br /> <br /> EDIT: And if Secrets of the Tribes is going to be a thing, maybe we'd get some neat updates or looks on their favoured prey and their preferred strategies of engaging in Siskur-Dah.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-18T21:42:49-07:00","id":1131118,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1131020-night-horrors-shunned-by-the-moon?p=1131116#post1131116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure how I feel about getting a Night Horrors book that's focused, primarily, on other werewolves, but the Pure and Bale Hounds need some love.</div> </div> </div> </div>The first chapter of the first one was all about werewolves. And a lot of people seem to think Ghost Wolf means 'werewolves with all the benefits of Forsaken but not tied down by the tribes,' when it's actually more distant than that and they tend to round out the whole freakshow between Forsaken and Pure and outside of both, like those in the Temple of Apollo. More enemies would be great, but once these guys are out we have Hosts, Claimed, and Spirits, which seems like they would fit in their own book.<br /> <br /> Of course, that does require the book to be made and all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> EDIT: And if Secrets of the Tribes is going to be a thing, maybe we'd get some neat updates or looks on their favoured prey and their preferred strategies of engaging in Siskur-Dah. </div> </div> </div>Based on every other 'Secrets of' I'm guessing it will be mostly in-character stuff with a few pages of mechanics in the back. I really wouldn't expect huge new changes to material there but it would certainly be a good way to show off things like tribal initiations, how tribes deal with their prey differently and how they deal with their non-sacred prey when its an issue, and so forth.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-18T21:52:31-07:00","id":1131122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1131020-night-horrors-shunned-by-the-moon?p=1131118#post1131118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The first chapter of the first one was all about werewolves. And a lot of people seem to think Ghost Wolf means 'werewolves with all the benefits of Forsaken but not tied down by the tribes,' when it's actually more distant than that and they tend to round out the whole freakshow between Forsaken and Pure and outside of both, like those in the Temple of Apollo. More enemies would be great, but once these guys are out we have Hosts, Claimed, and Spirits, which seems like they would fit in their own book.<br /> <br /> Of course, that does require the book to be made and all.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is a very good point. I <i>did </i>like the Temple of Apollo quite a bit, and if I had to hazard a guess I imagine the Lodge of the Field would be a Ghost Wolf Lodge too. Thinking about it that way, you could have a lot of opportunity for very weird, but also very cool, werewolf societies going on and that's always neat.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1131020-night-horrors-shunned-by-the-moon?p=1131118#post1131118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Based on every other 'Secrets of' I'm guessing it will be mostly in-character stuff with a few pages of mechanics in the back. I really wouldn't expect huge new changes to material there but it would certainly be a good way to show off things like tribal initiations, how tribes deal with their prey differently and how they deal with their non-sacred prey when its an issue, and so forth.</div> </div> </div> </div>If it's anything like <b>Secrets of the Covenants</b>, I'd be good with that. The fluff there really helped me figure out the mindset of some of the Covenants and helped emphasize them as philosophies as opposed to organizations. The Carthian chapter, in particular, did a really good job at showing the different faces of that Covenant, while the Invictus chapter did a good job of presenting them as something a little more interesting than &quot;The Establishment&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-18T22:18:31-07:00","id":1131126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1131020-night-horrors-shunned-by-the-moon?p=1131122#post1131122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That is a very good point. I <i>did </i>like the Temple of Apollo quite a bit, and if I had to hazard a guess I imagine the Lodge of the Field would be a Ghost Wolf Lodge too. Thinking about it that way, you could have a lot of opportunity for very weird, but also very cool, werewolf societies going on and that's always neat.<br /> <br /> [COLOR=#252C2F][FONT=Helvetica][SIZE=13px]<br /> <br /> If it's anything like <b>Secrets of the Covenants</b>, I'd be good with that. The fluff there really helped me figure out the mindset of some of the Covenants and helped emphasize them as philosophies as opposed to organizations. The Carthian chapter, in particular, did a really good job at showing the different faces of that Covenant, while the Invictus chapter did a good job of presenting them as something a little more interesting than &amp;quot;The Establishment&amp;quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's exactly why I'm excited to see Ghost Wolves here. I love the Lodge of the Fields and Temple of Apollo and hope this fleshes them out. And I hope we get some type of stats for Lycon-Ur plus art. The ones Chris posted online are fucking scary!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T05:51:11-07:00","id":1131219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1131020-night-horrors-shunned-by-the-moon?p=1131116#post1131116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure how I feel about getting a Night Horrors book that's focused, primarily, on other werewolves, but the Pure and Bale Hounds need some love. The update to the Pure in Forsaken By Rome was very nice, but it doesn't give them any new Shadow Gifts or Wolf Gifts, which would have been interesting to see. Also, if we get Bale Hounds updated, we might get to see what an Infernal/Lower Depths Ephemeral Being looks like, even if it's just a template the way Abyssal Being is now.<br /> <br /> EDIT: And if Secrets of the Tribes is going to be a thing, maybe we'd get some neat updates or looks on their favoured prey and their preferred strategies of engaging in Siskur-Dah.</div> </div> </div> </div> I think its likely that we will get servants and allies of the Ghost Wolves, Balehounds, and Pure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T07:15:14-07:00","id":1131259,"title":"","content":"As Rich mentioned it at GenCon, I figured <a href=\"https://www.zeropointinformation.com/blog/2017/stepping-back/\" target=\"_blank\">I should make it public</a>.<br /> <br /> <b>TL; DR: </b>Yes, I'm not developer any more. No, it's not to do with one line against the other. It's all to do with the amount of work at my day-job.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>--<br /> Stew Wilson<br /> Werewolf Developer<br /> <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/index.php?manufacturers_id=3820&amp;affiliate_id=81234\" target=\"_blank\">My games. Buy them.</a><br /> The maturity of the developer might go down as well as up. Bum. Willy. Fart. Nietzche.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28-digitalraven","name":"DigitalRaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T07:59:33-07:00","id":1131276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1131020-night-horrors-shunned-by-the-moon?p=1131032#post1131032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This poor, maligned, abandoned gameline! Those evil devs starving it of content!<br /> <br /> I kid, I kid. Very surprised and excited to see Ghost Wolves rolled up in this; I've always liked them more than the Tribes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup, its suffering from malnutrition that only a antagonist gallery can rectify.<br /> <br /> But when you look at Ghost Wolves, unless you're a player portraying one... the games almost go out of their way to portray the poor misguided Ghost Wolves as a horrible problem just waiting to happen, there can be no other way really.<br /> <br /> From the Lodge of the Field to Bale Hounds to the Deceiver Lune.. the sad fact is that Ghost Wolves have endless potential to be exploited and warped into unwitting antagonists... and I love it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1686,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","user":"Korogra","date":". 08-19-2017, 11:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T08:42:00-07:00","id":1131287,"title":"","content":"I don't think Bale Hounds count as Ghost Wolves do they?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T08:48:22-07:00","id":1131292,"title":"","content":"I'm looking forward to seeing what the Bale Hounds perferred Prey is. <br /> <br /> Anyone want to guess what a Bale Hound of Lust preferred prey is? Hehehehe. Quadmire the Werewolf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T08:55:20-07:00","id":1131295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1131020-night-horrors-shunned-by-the-moon?p=1131287#post1131287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think Bale Hounds count as Ghost Wolves do they?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you run them as a Lodge, they technically come from every tribe, though some are undoubtedly Ghost Wolves.<br /> <br /> If you run them as a Tribe well.. they are a tribe, though they will still infiltrate the other factions just the same.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T09:22:41-07:00","id":1131309,"title":"","content":"Ghost Wolves are werewolves who haven't joined up with one of the five tribes, but also aren't members of the Pure.<br /> <br /> Some tend towards the Forsaken tribes, like the Eaters of the Dead who were trying to become a new Forsaken tribe. But most are completely on their own, maybe they don't know about the tribes, or reject them, maybe they've been suborned by another entity like Apollo, maybe they're part of some strange personality cult like the Field of Dogs, or they're just outside of everything and have their own agenda, like the Cull. Werewolves who aren't a part of something bigger, who don't get the education and support of the tribes, tend to become influenced by strange entities that know them better than they know themselves.<br /> <br /> As mentioned, a lot of people look at Ghost Wolves as 'Forsaken, but without any restrictions.' When in actuality they're the unknown quantities. This is why they're treated with distrust. Sure maybe they just don't like the tribe thing, but it's also possible, even more possible, that they work for a soul-stealing abomination and are just trying to get close to your pack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T10:22:50-07:00","id":1131341,"title":"","content":"They called themselves the 9th tribe so I'm inclined to think of them as a tribe not Ghost Wolves. <br /> <br /> One thing that would be interesting is if the Bale Hound section has rules for Maeljin and Bale Hound corrupted Wolf Blooded (Bale Blooded?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T12:16:23-07:00","id":1131379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1131020-night-horrors-shunned-by-the-moon?p=1131309#post1131309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ghost Wolves are werewolves who haven't joined up with one of the five tribes, but also aren't members of the Pure.<br /> <br /> Some tend towards the Forsaken tribes, like the Eaters of the Dead who were trying to become a new Forsaken tribe. But most are completely on their own, maybe they don't know about the tribes, or reject them, maybe they've been suborned by another entity like Apollo, maybe they're part of some strange personality cult like the Field of Dogs, or they're just outside of everything and have their own agenda, like the Cull. Werewolves who aren't a part of something bigger, who don't get the education and support of the tribes, tend to become influenced by strange entities that know them better than they know themselves.<br /> <br /> As mentioned, a lot of people look at Ghost Wolves as 'Forsaken, but without any restrictions.' When in actuality they're the unknown quantities. This is why they're treated with distrust. Sure maybe they just don't like the tribe thing, but it's also possible, even more possible, that they work for a soul-stealing abomination and are just trying to get close to your pack.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right. Why would I swear not to eat people when they're totally fucking delicious?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T12:19:12-07:00","id":1131382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1131020-night-horrors-shunned-by-the-moon?p=1131341#post1131341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They called themselves the 9th tribe so I'm inclined to think of them as a tribe not Ghost Wolves.</div> </div> </div> </div>They were given three different options to play, only one of them was as the ninth tribe. If you played them as lodges or using the Dark Pantheism option, they would be ghost wolves.<br /> <br /> I'm hoping we get a mix of them this time around, one can have a Ninth Tribe following Viruhk-Ur, and other lodges following the Maeljin.<br /> <br /> It's all in the last chapter of <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/3418/Blasphemies?it=1\" target=\"_blank\">Blasphemies, a great book I suggest you pick up</a>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 08-19-2017, 03:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T14:23:57-07:00","id":1131440,"title":"","content":"I am wondering how the new rules would interact with Bale hounds. In 1st edition they had a fetish and rite to allows them to fake harmony 5 but now? <br /> <br /> I am wondering whats the use of flayed lunes now? In 1st they taught you the secret gifts of &quot;Tainted moon&quot; and the not so secret &quot;Eclipse gifts&quot; but from what the former Dev of Werewolf have stated there is no more &quot;x tribe only gifts&quot; so this opens the question about what their use. <br /> <br /> Considering that the Bale hounds can pretend to be other tribes, meaning the can lie to spirits about their &quot;patron&quot;, then it would be weird if all the flayed lunes did was teach balehounds their lunar gifts. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T14:36:55-07:00","id":1131442,"title":"","content":"Their rite let Soulless Wolf take their Harmony loss instead of them. It's still something that can be used now, to keep them at Harmony 5 when having Breaking Points left and right.<br /> <br /> Tainted Moon gifts weren't tribe only, they were just hard to get. Technically other people can get flayed lunes, they're just not likely to, the Pure because they hate lunes, the Forsaken because they like them. Right now it would likely just be an alternative set of Moon Gifts, like Screaming Moon.. Incidentally the Eclipse gifts weren't tribal only and weren't taught by flayed lunes, 'The Bale Hounds don't have a monopoly on the concept of darkness or shadows.'<br /> <br /> They couldn't necessarily pretend to be members of other tribes, especially with the abundance of 'tell me about this target' powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 08-19-2017, 05:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T14:41:22-07:00","id":1131445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1131020-night-horrors-shunned-by-the-moon?p=1131442#post1131442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tainted Moon gifts weren't tribe only, they were just hard to get. Technically other people can get flayed lunes, they're just not likely to, the Pure because they hate lunes, the Forsaken because they like them.<br /> <br /> Also the Eclipse gifts weren't tribal only and weren't taught by flayed lunes.<br /> <br /> They couldn't necessarily pretend to be members of other tribes, especially with the abundance of 'tell me about this target' powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>I remember the Eclipse gifts being while rare not tribe only but i though the Tainted moon were Balehound only. About the pretending, i meant belonging to a tribe while still being balehounds, instead of being able to pretend to be either Pure at one time or Forsaken in another time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T14:46:56-07:00","id":1131449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1131020-night-horrors-shunned-by-the-moon?p=1131445#post1131445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I remember the Eclipse gifts being while rare not tribe only but i though the Tainted moon were Balehound only. About the pretending, i meant belonging to a tribe while still being balehounds, instead of being able to pretend to be either Pure at one time or Forsaken in another time.</div> </div> </div> </div>The flayed lune rite, the one to get a flayed lune, is only taught to Bale Hounds. There are tribe and lodge-only rites in second edition. But you could potentially use it outside of the Bale Hounds.<br /> <br /> Belonging to a tribe while being a bale hound is easy and doesn't require any special powers. Olivia Citysmith is one, as is one in the Pure book. If you join the Bale Hounds as a Lodge like in the Lodge of Mammon, you're already there.<br /> <br /> But moving from Pure to Forsaken and back against isn't something that was mentioned in the books. If it pops up it's pretty easy to just have a ritual of deceit that would turn ones silvery renown brands into red and burning ones for the Pure, and the other way around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 08-19-2017, 05:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T14:53:01-07:00","id":1131453,"title":"","content":"I think this will be the case, but here's hoping that they will follow the format for Beast's Night Horrors book, namely a decent chunk of pages that explore the characters of each chapter before getting to the NPCs. <br /> <br /> We could use both mechanics and fluff for all of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T14:55:34-07:00","id":1131456,"title":"","content":"[QUOTE=Cinder;n1131453]but here's hoping that they will follow the format for Beast's Night Horrors book, namely a decent chunk of pages that explore the characters of each chapter before getting to the NPCs./QUOTE]<br /> <br /> Havent read the Nights horror for Beast, what do you mean on &quot;explore the character before getting to the NPCs&quot;? <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T14:58:21-07:00","id":1131458,"title":"","content":"Show a bunch of example Pure, Bale Hounds and Ghost Wolves before showing the mechanics for them. Like if you look at Night Horrors: Wolfsbane, the idigam section has a bunch of mechanics for idigam, then gets into some specific idigam using those mechanics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T15:02:17-07:00","id":1131461,"title":"","content":"[QUOTE=LokiRavenSpeak;n1131456]<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1131020-night-horrors-shunned-by-the-moon?p=1131453#post1131453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">but here's hoping that they will follow the format for Beast's Night Horrors book, namely a decent chunk of pages that explore the characters of each chapter before getting to the NPCs./QUOTE]<br /> <br /> Havent read the Nights horror for Beast, what do you mean on &quot;explore the character before getting to the NPCs&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>Beast had three chapters, Heroes, Beasts and Insatiables. The Night Horror's format is that of a collection of NPCs but, in some cases like that one of Beast, the chapter does not begin with them. Heroes are described in more depth, building upon what's written about them in the core, while Insatiables, being a new kind of antagonists, are described and given their own mechanics.<br /> <br /> My hope, which I guess will be fullfilled, is that we get some informations and 2nd Edition rules (Gifts and so on) for these three kind of wolves as well. Not&quot;only&quot; a list of NPCs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T15:07:30-07:00","id":1131463,"title":"","content":"Oh, yeah i hope they go that route too","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T16:25:57-07:00","id":1131498,"title":"","content":"Relistened to the, panel Shunned by the Moon will also explore the Myths, Legends, and Hunting Grounds for Ghost Wolves, Pure, and Bale Hounds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T16:35:30-07:00","id":1131504,"title":"","content":"That sounds like Secrets of the Tribes.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Okay it's about Shunned by the Moon, 'all enemies of the tribes with their own myths, legends and hunting grounds will be detailed in this book.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 08-19-2017, 07:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T06:37:51-07:00","id":1131684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DigitalRaven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1131020-night-horrors-shunned-by-the-moon?p=1131259#post1131259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As Rich mentioned it at GenCon, I figured <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.zeropointinformation.com/blog/2017/stepping-back/&amp;quot;]I</a> should make it public[/URL].<br /> <br /> <b>TL; DR: </b>Yes, I'm not developer any more. No, it's not to do with one line against the other. It's all to do with the amount of work at my day-job.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's really sad to read about Stew' step down. <br /> <br /> So, umm, who's at the steering wheel right now?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/216-zooroos","name":"Zooroos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar216_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"250"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T08:10:58-07:00","id":1131721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zooroos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1131020-night-horrors-shunned-by-the-moon?p=1131684#post1131684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's really sad to read about Stew' step down.<br /> <br /> So, umm, who's at the steering wheel right now?</div> </div> </div> </div>The answer seems self evident.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T09:58:37-07:00","id":1131762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DigitalRaven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1131020-night-horrors-shunned-by-the-moon?p=1131259#post1131259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As Rich mentioned it at GenCon, I figured <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.zeropointinformation.com/blog/2017/stepping-back/&amp;quot;]I</a> should make it public[/URL].<br /> <br /> <b>TL; DR: </b>Yes, I'm not developer any more. No, it's not to do with one line against the other. It's all to do with the amount of work at my day-job.</div> </div> </div> </div>Much thanks for your awesome work, Stew. You took Werewolf from being the CofD game I liked least to being the one I can't wait to play (again!), and getting to work on The Pack was some of the most fun I've had on a book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T10:33:02-07:00","id":1131777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zooroos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1131020-night-horrors-shunned-by-the-moon?p=1131684#post1131684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, umm, who's at the steering wheel right now?</div> </div> </div> </div>No one, it sounds like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T11:17:24-07:00","id":1131793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1131020-night-horrors-shunned-by-th