">Have another teaser! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <i>Look, this is the hard, cold truth. The Cull are coming. They\u2019re coming, and nothing we can do will stop that. Now, we either give them the weakest as a sacrifice so the rest of us can live, or we all die. Me? I plan to live.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Looks like the Cull ain't no one's fool","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-05T08:41:40-07:00","id":1251675,"title":"","content":"So with the mention of both the Cull and the Devourers, can we assume that Ghost Wolves divides themselves more or less according to the same factions as the Uratha did in the Neolithic Era? (I mean, there are 7 sects in Sundered World, with two of them serving as the foundation for the future Pure/Forsaken. It makes sense that the rest would be a Ghost Wolf territory)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-05T08:59:03-07:00","id":1251679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1131020-night-horrors-shunned-by-the-moon?p=1251675#post1251675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So with the mention of both the Cull and the Devourers, can we assume that Ghost Wolves divides themselves more or less according to the same factions as the Uratha did in the Neolithic Era? (I mean, there are 7 sects in Sundered World, with two of them serving as the foundation for the future Pure/Forsaken. It makes sense that the rest would be a Ghost Wolf territory)</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't assume that, no - among other things, the Cull and the Devourers are both part of the same entry in Shunned.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-05T10:15:44-07:00","id":1251694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1131020-night-horrors-shunned-by-the-moon?p=1251660#post1251660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have another teaser! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <i>Look, this is the hard, cold truth. The Cull are coming. They\u2019re coming, and nothing we can do will stop that. Now, we either give them the weakest as a sacrifice so the rest of us can live, or we all die. Me? I plan to live.</i></div> </div> </div> </div><i>I cull the herd. It's what I do.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-05T10:37:44-07:00","id":1251703,"title":"","content":"Is this Cull more in the vein of the 'twisted Daoism of the monstrous Cull in China' mentioned in the Pack? You said they were not like the Pangaean Cull.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-05T11:08:45-07:00","id":1251716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1131020-night-horrors-shunned-by-the-moon?p=1251675#post1251675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So with the mention of both the Cull and the Devourers, can we assume that Ghost Wolves divides themselves more or less according to the same factions as the Uratha did in the Neolithic Era? (I mean, there are 7 sects in Sundered World, with two of them serving as the foundation for the future Pure/Forsaken. It makes sense that the rest would be a Ghost Wolf territory)</div> </div> </div> </div>The Shepherds seem to be precursors to the Iron Masters. The Mourners are probably obsolete, given that Pangaea no longer exists -- although they may have spawned secret lodges dedicated to the mysteries of the Gauntlet. The Tyrants were never an organized faction at all. The Maw probably have the most potential as modern-day antagonists -- maybe they're allied with the Devourers, or maybe they're the Devourers' rivals?<br /> <br /> I could also see a niche for a faction of Ghost Wolves who reject Uratha society completely and are seeking a cure for their &quot;curse.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/40-dspaul","name":"DSPaul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-05T11:15:42-07:00","id":1251720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1131020-night-horrors-shunned-by-the-moon?p=1251703#post1251703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is this Cull more in the vein of the 'twisted Daoism of the monstrous Cull in China' mentioned in the Pack? You said they were not like the Pangaean Cull.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's the same Cull, although with some additional development past the original throwaway line in The Pack.<br /> <br /> See, the Pangaean Cull wanted to cull humanity. That's not what the modern Cull is about...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-05T11:24:07-07:00","id":1251722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DSPaul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1131020-night-horrors-shunned-by-the-moon?p=1251716#post1251716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Mourners are probably obsolete, given that Pangaea no longer exists -- although they may have spawned secret lodges dedicated to the mysteries of the Gauntlet.</div> </div> </div> </div>They sort of got what they wanted, though. Pangaea is separated from the rest of the world, it may well exist just beyond the reach of werewolves. It's possible they're somewhere in there, partying it up in ancient settlements prepared for their isolation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1131020-night-horrors-shunned-by-the-moon?p=1251720#post1251720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's the same Cull, although with some additional development past the original throwaway line in The Pack.<br /> <br /> See, the Pangaean Cull wanted to cull humanity. That's not what the modern Cull is about...</div> </div> </div> </div>Really looking forward to seeing it.<br /> <br /> As a fan of lodges, and someone who's enjoyed the assorted lodges we've seen (in the Pack and homebrewed), are there lodges in the book, with a lodge write-up? Or are the factions separate from that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-05T11:45:43-07:00","id":1251728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1131020-night-horrors-shunned-by-the-moon?p=1251722#post1251722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really looking forward to seeing it.<br /> <br /> As a fan of lodges, and someone who's enjoyed the assorted lodges we've seen (in the Pack and homebrewed), are there lodges in the book, with a lodge write-up? Or are the factions separate from that?</div> </div> </div> </div>No Lodges - the Ghost Wolf entries are separate from that. Lodges are alluded to or indicated as possible outcomes for some entries though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-05T12:29:57-07:00","id":1251738,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1131020-night-horrors-shunned-by-the-moon?p=1251728#post1251728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No Lodges - the Ghost Wolf entries are separate from that. Lodges are alluded to or indicated as possible outcomes for some entries though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay cool, it's nice to have something to work off of.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-05T14:40:28-07:00","id":1251762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1131020-night-horrors-shunned-by-the-moon?p=1251728#post1251728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No Lodges - the Ghost Wolf entries are separate from that. Lodges are alluded to or indicated as possible outcomes for some entries though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like you made unofficial <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1173539-eight-pure-a-weeping?p=1174629#post1174629\">Lodge out of Mourners</a>?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>The Mourners<br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">\u200bClaws of Samsara, Mercykillers, Sin Eaters</span></span></b></span><br /> <i>Months since the First Change have done nothing to calm his sleep. Each night sees the same maelstrom of nightmares and a sense of lurking fear chewing at the corners of his awareness. He stirs from slumber, but the figments of his dream seem to have chased him right into the waking world; a looming shadow, perched at the end of his bed, remains resolutely real. &quot;I'm so sorry,&quot; it says, heavy with grief. &quot;For all of this. But we can still save you.&quot; Just like his nightmares always did, it ends in swift motion, then blood.</i><br /> <br /> The Mourners are the newest incarnation of an old Lodge, a lineage of self-martyring and sin-eating cults that has cropped up round the world over and over again under different names, the tenets a little different each time. Like their forebears, the Mourners focus their hunt upon what some would see as easy prey - newly fledged Forsaken, the freshly Changed in their early months or years before their spirits are carved under a tapestry of renown. The so-called Mercykillers' hunt is not one of savage glory; even as they wring necks and cut throats, they weep for those they slay. Mourners are prone to fits of overt self-punishment and mortification, girding themselves for the hunt with guilt over killing other Uratha and staining themselves with sin so that others need not.<br /> <br /> \u200bThe public face of the Mourner creed has it that a young werewolf's soul can be saved, but that those who have committed many deeds in service to the Moon, and hence been branded deeply by it, cannot find redemption with their souls so marred. Outsider Pure are often confused as to the exact nature of Mourner beliefs - whether they believe in a wheel of reincarnation, or that 'pure' souls not deeply marked by the Moon will pass on to strengthen the Wolf instead, or various other theories. Regardless, to the Mourners, their homicidal approach to lesser Forsaken is a necessity born from the fact that most <i>Urdaga</i><u>\u200b<i>\u200b</i></u>\u200b will never turn to the Pure regardless of torture or persuasion, and that every day a Forsaken remains in the moon-faith they creep closer to their souls being forever lost. The Mourners, for their part, believe they act as scalpels to cut away the spiritual purity that can yet be saved, killing out of kindness. Each Mourner accepts that their actions cost their own soul - but better that a scant few Mercykillers are condemned, if many times that number of Forsaken are cleft from the moonlight before it taints them forever.<br /> <br /> Mourners usually prefer stealth, infiltration and covert activity, isolating victims rather than seeking direct confrontation. To the Forsaken, Mourners are like bogeymen - murderous assassins insane or self-delusional enough to pretend sorrow even as they slay kin in violation of the Wolf's laws. To the Pure, Mourners are often a problem - they clash with Fire-Touched preachers trying to convert the Forsaken, their self-martyring manner and the lowly nature of their chosen prey disgusts many, and there are lingering suspicions they hide deviant beliefs behind their outwardly fanatical fa\u00e7ade. Still, Pure warlords value them as adept killers who have overcome qualms against killing other Uratha, particularly the lesser and less-threatening Forsaken that many Pure footsoldiers may hesitate to actually slay - making Mercykillers valuable agents of terror. Mourners also sometimes serve as sin-eater priests for other Pure on their deathbeds, and they have some appeal to Pure packs who want the moral comfort of shifting the guilt for killing Forsaken onto a willing recipient. <br /> <br /> \u200bWith less than a decade since the current incarnation of the Lodge formed, it is small and has only eight members across north America and east Asia. Half are Fire-Touched; the others are Tribeless Pure, scourged of their Auspices but unaffiliated with any Firstborn. These Ghost Wolves are devoted entirely to the Lodge, and possibly nurture dreams of future Tribehood. New candidates are being considered for the Lodge's ranks; the Lodge offers rationalisation and purpose to Uratha who feel self-loathing for what they have become or the terrible things they have done since their First Change. Most of the potential new Mourners are Fire-Touched or Purified Ghost Wolves, and the current adherents vet for inclinations towards the sort of careful, deadly approach to 'freeing' the new Forsaken that suits the Lodge's tenets. However, an Indian branch of Ivory Claws recently came into contact with the Mourners and, noting similarities to an older and extinct Indian Lodge that self-destructed spectacularly over a century ago, have become suspicious. <i>Tzuumfin</i>\u200b agents are investigating to see if their concerns are legitimate; one is petitioning for membership. Her elders think she is going to serve them as a double-agent; she's actually trying to dupe both sides, hoping to resurrect the older Lodge that her own grandparents were among the final adherents of. </div> </div> </div>More in the linked post itself. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-06T04:29:16-07:00","id":1251882,"title":"","content":"Another teaser: the first coupla paragraphs from the Mimics entry!<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Children of Change: The Mimics</b></span><br /> Evolution is a bitch. Uratha have been top dog for thousands of years, the handiwork of big daddy Wolf, and sure, they\u2019ve done a passable job, but it\u2019s time to step aside. Get out of the way for the new kids on the block, the latest models built to actually win this war. The age of Forsaken and Firstborn is over; it\u2019s time to throw the obsolete and the outdated into the trash. The Uratha had their chance to pass the mantle of the hunt on to the mimics, and they failed, so now the mimics will take it by force.<br /> <br /> Mimics are insane. Each mimic is a shapechanger without compare, the quicksilver foundations of the werewolf fine-tuned into overdrive. They\u2019re the handiwork of a curious and clever force who may, this time, have overstepped the mark. A mimic\u2019s shivering flesh and bone make it the perfect doppelg\u00e4nger \u2014 hiding as anything, anywhere, in a chameleon seeming. This mercurial mastery comes at a cost to mind and spirit, though, and it doesn\u2019t help that the phratries \u2014 the surviving packs of mimics \u2014 are convinced of their superiority over other werewolves and filled with rage and spite.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-06T04:36:23-07:00","id":1251884,"title":"","content":"<img src=\"https://media.giphy.com/media/dfrpQANpFMhHy/giphy.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Isn't she pretty?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-06T06:28:20-07:00","id":1251900,"title":"","content":"Well, time to teach my players not to go anywhere without wolf senses active. EVER.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3347-wild-eyes","name":"Wild-Eyes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-06T14:23:14-07:00","id":1252008,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1131020-night-horrors-shunned-by-the-moon?p=1251882#post1251882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another teaser: the first coupla paragraphs from the Mimics entry!<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Children of Change: The Mimics</b></span><br /> Evolution is a bitch. Uratha have been top dog for thousands of years, the handiwork of big daddy Wolf, and sure, they\u2019ve done a passable job, but it\u2019s time to step aside. Get out of the way for the new kids on the block, the latest models built to actually win this war. The age of Forsaken and Firstborn is over; it\u2019s time to throw the obsolete and the outdated into the trash. The Uratha had their chance to pass the mantle of the hunt on to the mimics, and they failed, so now the mimics will take it by force.<br /> <br /> Mimics are insane. Each mimic is a shapechanger without compare, the quicksilver foundations of the werewolf fine-tuned into overdrive. They\u2019re the handiwork of a curious and clever force who may, this time, have overstepped the mark. A mimic\u2019s shivering flesh and bone make it the perfect doppelg\u00e4nger \u2014 hiding as anything, anywhere, in a chameleon seeming. This mercurial mastery comes at a cost to mind and spirit, though, and it doesn\u2019t help that the phratries \u2014 the surviving packs of mimics \u2014 are convinced of their superiority over other werewolves and filled with rage and spite.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was already happy that a new Forsaken book was coming out, now you've gone got me hyped!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/427-rahuman101","name":"Rahuman101","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar427_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-07T07:28:02-07:00","id":1252210,"title":"","content":"<br /> Another teaser for Shunned - this time the opening paragraphs of the Devourers!<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>The Culling: Ghost Wolf Devourers</b><br /> <br /> At the turn of the 21st century, a nightmare from stories poured into reality. The so-called Cull erupted in Russian and Chinese territories in an orgy of brutality and cannibalistic transgression. They plucked secrets from gristle and viscera, wielding incredible power torn from the corpses of their victims. The Cull swore allegiance to no Tribe and fought Pure and Forsaken alike. In a scant few years since, they have hauled themselves up to become a major faction in the region, pursuing a relentless assault that is only strengthened by each victim they tear apart and consume. They rally under a mad philosophy of the winnowing of the People. There are too many werewolves, they say, the natural force of predation run wild and weak. Like Father Wolf, the Uratha of today have stumbled from greatness through the spreading of their Essence. If balance is to be restored, many must be culled.<br /> <br /> Until the Cull, most werewolves knew little of devourers. Walking a blood-drenched path to profane enlightenment by tearing divinity from the entrails of their fellows, these cannibal witches hail from ancient practices that had dwindled to almost nothing in the present day. A scant few practitioners persisted, scattered across the world and passing the sinister rite down to trusted students. Each of the traditional devourers is an iron-willed sorcerer of flesh and spirit, their soul carved in mimicry of the hunger that drives spirits to consume each other.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-07T07:37:46-07:00","id":1252212,"title":"","content":"Have I ever mentioned that I love cannibalistic black magic? I utterly adore cannibalistic black magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3347-wild-eyes","name":"Wild-Eyes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-07T08:51:17-07:00","id":1252226,"title":"","content":"Devourers are exactly what I was hoping for! Mimics seem extremely cool as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/40-dspaul","name":"DSPaul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-07T17:20:50-07:00","id":1252398,"title":"","content":"How exciting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-09T05:15:47-07:00","id":1252725,"title":"","content":"We don't want Ghost Wolves having all the werewolf-devouring fun, do we? Here's an excerpt from one of the new Bale Hounds Maeljin:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The servants of <i>Lakh\u2019ma</i> make even other Bale Hounds uneasy, for they are the eaters of werewolves. Where every Uratha lives with the temptation to eat the flesh of humans, wolves, and werewolves for power, they work to resist for the sake of the balance of their own souls. Those who follow <i>Lakh\u2019ma</i> revel in feasting on the forbidden meats. Whenever possible, the successful hunts ends with the Bale Hound drinking the blood of the fallen and stripping the flesh from their bones. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-09T05:30:28-07:00","id":1252730,"title":"","content":"\u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1131020-night-horrors-shunned-by-the-moon?p=1250779#post1250779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bale Hounds are no longer divided up by their allegiance to Maeljin dedicated to corruption of human values (ie the Vices Plus Two of the old approach) - instead, they're defined by the corruption of particular *Uratha* values.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1131020-night-horrors-shunned-by-the-moon?p=1252725#post1252725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b<br /> <i>The servants of </i><i>Lakh\u2019ma</i><i> make even other Bale Hounds uneasy, for they are the eaters of werewolves. Where every Uratha lives with the temptation to eat the flesh of humans, wolves, and werewolves for power, they work to resist for the sake of the balance of their own souls. Those who follow </i><i>Lakh\u2019ma</i><i> revel in feasting on the forbidden meats. Whenever possible, the successful hunts ends with the Bale Hound drinking the blood of the fallen and stripping the flesh from their bones.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bSo Maelijn of Hunger ( Or Gluttony ) we have left in 2E - even if name changed from <i>Baalphegor</i> to <i>Lakh\u2019ma</i>. Hm... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Seeing as 'Not Starving' is not Renown of Uratha - I have a question then:<br /> <br /> <b>I'm guessing well that 2E Bale Hounds are about dedicating to break particular Oath of Moon ( and possible Oath of Urfarah ) - so Hounds of Lakh\u2019ma are breaking </b><i><b>Nu Hu Uzu Eren \u2014 Do Not Eat The Flesh Of Man Or Wolf? </b></i><b>And others Bale Hounds are breaking other Oaths?</b><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-09T06:05:48-07:00","id":1252734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1131020-night-horrors-shunned-by-the-moon?p=1252730#post1252730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b\u200bSo Maelijn of Hunger ( Or Gluttony ) we have left in 2E - even if name changed from <i>Baalphegor</i> to <i>Lakh\u2019ma</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can see how you've reached that conclusion, but nope. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Edit: It's not a name change, no.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1131020-night-horrors-shunned-by-the-moon?p=1252730#post1252730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b\u200b<br /> <b>I'm guessing well that 2E Bale Hounds are about dedicating to break particular Oath of Moon ( and possible Oath of Urfarah ) - so Hounds of Lakh\u2019ma are breaking </b><i><b>Nu Hu Uzu Eren \u2014 Do Not Eat The Flesh Of Man Or Wolf? </b></i><b>And others Bale Hounds are breaking other Oaths?</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Not quite, no. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-09T06:53:48-07:00","id":1252745,"title":"","content":"If there's no focus on 7+2 sins then Baalphegor and the others are unlikely to have any relevance.<br /> Lakh'ma seems to be either a (collection of) Maeljin, or a more abstract concept. <i>If</i> the Bale Hounds are divided by Renown (each category of Bale Hounds trying to corrupt a specific Renown) then Lakh'ma could represent/be anti-Purity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-09T06:58:25-07:00","id":1252746,"title":"","content":"It seems more like there are many more maeljin in 2e than in 1e- I assume we still have the big 9, but they are much more detach (and less relevant) than those who actively work to disrupt the lives of the specific supernatural monster in question (like, instead of nine gods of sin, you have a full pantheon of evil, with the first nine serving as either mortal or general evils, while other demon gods work to corrupt other supernatural beings)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-09T07:19:44-07:00","id":1252755,"title":"","content":"Having separate &quot;choirs&quot; of evils for separate types of supernatural creatures seems weird to me. I'd rather have that Infernal demons focus on inverting their victims' held virtues, which would explain why Bale Hounds are naturally defined by Uratha values without having specific werewolf demons. And wouldn't put a divide between Bale Hounds and Wound-spirits since Uratha and spirits have wildly different values to corrupt.<br /> Or Maeljin might be completely separate from Inferno, which would be fine by me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-09T07:28:23-07:00","id":1252759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1131020-night-horrors-shunned-by-the-moon?p=1252730#post1252730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b<br /> <b>I'm guessing well that 2E Bale Hounds are about dedicating to break particular Oath of Moon ( and possible Oath of Urfarah ) - so Hounds of Lakh\u2019ma are breaking </b><i><b>Nu Hu Uzu Eren \u2014 Do Not Eat The Flesh Of Man Or Wolf? </b></i><b>And others Bale Hounds are breaking other Oaths?</b></div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1131020-night-horrors-shunned-by-the-moon?p=1252734#post1252734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not quite, no. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><b>So maybe 2E Bale Hounds are about breaking ANY Ban Uratha takes and </b><b>corrup</b><b>ting them?</b> Oaths of Moon are example, Tribal Vows would also be another. I could also see then Bale Hounds that try to undermine Packs or Lodges Totems, to breaking their Bans - and so corrupting Totems themselves for Maeljinns...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 09-09-2018, 10:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-11T20:55:32-07:00","id":1253470,"title":"","content":"Note: Forsaken Tribal vows <b>are </b>a part of the Oath of the Moon. A specific part, but a part nonetheless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-12T07:00:33-07:00","id":1253577,"title":"","content":"Forsaken's moongifts are now (2nd edition) pretty powerful and a huge advantage for the forsaken.<br /> <br /> The gifts of the Anshega (blood, agony, hunger etc.) will be more powerful than the avarage shadow gifts ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-12T07:58:33-07:00","id":1253589,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Helur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1131020-night-horrors-shunned-by-the-moon?p=1253577#post1253577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The gifts of the Anshega (blood, agony, hunger etc.) will be more powerful than the avarage shadow gifts ?</div> </div> </div> </div>No; the new Gifts are Shadow Gifts, and are available to all Uratha in the same way as any other Shadow Gifts - the Pure Tribes just possess affinity for them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-12T13:51:08-07:00","id":1253696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1131020-night-horrors-shunned-by-the-moon?p=1250820#post1250820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> We're reviewing the Geryo mechanics at the moment so I'll let you know the answer once we've finished nailing everything down <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>anything new to report on this front?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-12T13:56:18-07:00","id":1253698,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1131020-night-horrors-shunned-by-the-moon?p=1253696#post1253696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">anything new to report on this front?</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019ll see if I can pull together a teaser after work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","cu