icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I for one got really excited when I heard that the book will also feature Lone Wolfs. The &amp;quot;Forsaken Chroniclers Guide - To Isolate&amp;quot; inspired some very unique WtF NPC in my group and I was wondering if we can expect something along those lines in Night Horrors? </div> </div> </div>What kind of thing are you looking for?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-06T11:46:52-07:00","id":1259260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1131020-night-horrors-shunned-by-the-moon?p=1259178#post1259178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What kind of thing are you looking for?</div> </div> </div> </div>First and foremost something like the Personal Totem to give Lone Wolfs something to flesh out their character rules- and fluffwise.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24674-micawber","name":"Micawber","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24674_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-06T13:39:52-07:00","id":1259277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1131020-night-horrors-shunned-by-the-moon?p=1258694#post1258694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> See for yourself.</div> </div> </div> </div>Did, and I actually didn\u2019t really enjoy either of them, but they definitely made me excited for the possibilities that Mimics and the Geryo can potentially represent","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-06T16:38:17-07:00","id":1259310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Micawber</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1131020-night-horrors-shunned-by-the-moon?p=1259260#post1259260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First and foremost something like the Personal Totem to give Lone Wolfs something to flesh out their character rules- and fluffwise.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, but I think you may have got some poor information about what\u2019s in this book. We\u2019re not looking to build in support for lone wolves nor include info on personal totems for characters. Totem rules were in The Pack.<br /> <br /> Shunned By The Moon is a Night Horrors book, which means its primary focus is antagonists and threats for characters to work against. Now, because quite a few Forsaken antagonists are also werewolves, Acrozatarim and I are being a bit sneaky and including rules so people can play some of these bad guys if they want. (And if it\u2019s what their Storyteller agrees to.) So you\u2019ll get more rules for fleshing out your Pure and Bale Hounds enemies \u2014 which also gives the toolkits for building and playing these characters as well.<br /> <br /> When you say \u2018Lone Wolves\u2019, are you talking about Ghost Wolves? We\u2019ve also included a few ways of making Ghost Wolves more of an antagonist threat for packs to hunt, but here they\u2019re mostly not really suitable for playable characters. These Uratha are generally truly broken \u2014 great threats, probably not as much fun to try and run as a character.<br /> <br /> With the spirits in the book, again these are designed as antagonists. There might be some of them who would be willing to work as totems but it\u2019s not going to be a pleasant relationship for the player. These things either (a) Hate Uratha and want to make them suffer, which means the player\u2019s going to be doing some messed up stuff to try and keep the abusive spirit happy, or (b) are alien enough that their wants and needs aren\u2019t really compatible with a Uratha trying to live the hunt.<br /> <br /> Beyond the werewolves and spirits, none of the humans, hosts, idigam or Geryo here are particularly looking for Uratha friends. Servants, maybe, slaves, possibly. Corpses, definitely.<br /> <br /> All in all, there\u2019s a ton of good stuff in this book. There\u2019s a ton of playable stuff that will add a lot of a chronicle, both for playable characters and antagonists. But this isn\u2019t the book to flesh out specific ways for playing a lone wolf chronicle, sorry.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-07T15:21:41-07:00","id":1259473,"title":"","content":"Dear <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar156_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"156\" data-vbnamecard=\"156\">Bunyip</a>. Can I know more about Ivory Claws in this book? Both powers and characters?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24222-acopiltaczet","name":"Acopiltaczet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24222_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-07T16:00:44-07:00","id":1259479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acopiltaczet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1131020-night-horrors-shunned-by-the-moon?p=1259473#post1259473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dear <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span>. Can I know more about Ivory Claws in this book? Both powers and characters?</div> </div> </div> </div>Acrozatarim talked a bit about them here: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1131020-night-horrors-shunned-by-the-moon?p=1251068#post1251068\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...68#post1251068</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-07T20:02:36-07:00","id":1259513,"title":"","content":"I don't know if this has been addressed yet, but will Bale hounds be considered the primary prey of blood talons, or will it be like how idigram, despite being spirits, are not prey under bone shadows due to being such an outside context threat","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-07T20:16:50-07:00","id":1259514,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1131020-night-horrors-shunned-by-the-moon?p=1259513#post1259513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know if this has been addressed yet, but will Bale hounds be considered the primary prey of blood talons, or will it be like how idigram, despite being spirits, are not prey under bone shadows due to being such an outside context threat</div> </div> </div> </div>Werewolves are the sacred prey of Blood Talons.<br /> <br /> All of them. <i>All of them</i>.<br /> <br /> The idigam don't count because the idigam break all the rules. Bale Hounds can't do that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-07T20:19:55-07:00","id":1259515,"title":"","content":"Ahh ok, thanks for the clarification.<br /> <br /> Damn I can't wait to see the Bale Hounds again","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-07T22:01:15-07:00","id":1259529,"title":"","content":"Will we see spirit cults in Shunned? Or would that already be covered by 'The Pack'?<br /> <br /> Tbh, I'm not sure we will even see many antagonistic Lodges for a while, given the 'recap the basics' doctrine for non-core material. Not saying it is a bad policy (it is a great idea) but that tends to eat up word count and the goal here is to add more and stranger bad guys with compelling story hooks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-07T22:16:30-07:00","id":1259531,"title":"","content":"There's spirits in it, and idigam and ridden of some sort, a cult could be built around any of them, if one isn't already written up. Even the hosts and werewolves could have cults. The Geryo don't seem like cult types, though that's just guesswork.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 10-08-2018, 01:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-08T08:27:52-07:00","id":1259601,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1131020-night-horrors-shunned-by-the-moon?p=1259514#post1259514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Werewolves are the sacred prey of Blood Talons.<br /> <br /> All of them. <i>All of them</i>.<br /> <br /> The idigam don't count because the idigam break all the rules. Bale Hounds can't do that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Kell I think you are having too much fun<br /> <br /> Dial it back to 11 before we all explode lol<br /> <br /> But since they hunt all of the werewolves(ALL OF THEM as you so accurately put it), do individual Blood Talons hunt themselves when there aren\u2019t any others around to keep themselves sharp? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1686,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","user":"Korogra","date":". 10-08-2018, 11:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.the