,{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-18T09:05:43-07:00","id":1261304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1131020-night-horrors-shunned-by-the-moon?p=1261299#post1261299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Weren't they in a book before? What do y'all think they do to the gauntlet? To me it seems they make fluid</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/419096-ukusgualu-the-lamprey-hosts\">They're newly canonized</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-18T10:40:13-07:00","id":1261324,"title":"","content":"Huh didn't know that, congrats Acrozatarim","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-18T11:26:18-07:00","id":1261332,"title":"","content":"That's pretty dang cool then, good for acrozatarim","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-18T14:57:59-07:00","id":1261393,"title":"","content":"The Lampreys are based off the notion I used back in that other thread, yeah; the concept's been refined and added to, and the Merovech mentioned in the preview provides a meaty sample Night Horror antagonist to hook the whole thing off.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-18T17:39:57-07:00","id":1261439,"title":"","content":"Must of been exciting to be able to canonize a creature you showed to the forums.<br /> <br /> I have one question, what would be the primary difference between how beshilu and lamprey host affect the gauntlet? At face value they are somewhat similar","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-19T00:12:26-07:00","id":1261498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1131020-night-horrors-shunned-by-the-moon?p=1261439#post1261439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Must of been exciting to be able to canonize a creature you showed to the forums.<br /> <br /> I have one question, what would be the primary difference between how beshilu and lamprey host affect the gauntlet? At face value they are somewhat similar</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> From the original thread, the Ukusgualu don't actually damage the Gauntlet. In fact, they repair it; if it's been brought down by Beshilu or thickened by Azlu, the blood they spit into it washes away the damage.<br /> <br /> Problem is, they <i>completely </i>repair it. As in, turn it back into a Border March, a revived relic of Pangaea-specifically, a callback to their old ocean, a red shifting river they immediately turn into their lair. Balance is maintained, but any attempt to cross needs to wade through the waters while dodging thirsty lampreys, and worse, the blood-water leaks out into the flesh; people affected by it become cultists of ancient blood gods even the Hosts aren't that familiar with. Plus, y'know, they can swim in it to teleport around and snatch people off the streets-or if they're especially pissed off, even move a locus around by shifting the tides.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","user":"Leliel","date":". 10-20-2018, 12:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-19T01:12:01-07:00","id":1261507,"title":"","content":"The Lamprey Hosts and their Gauntlet interactions have some specific implications for at least two of our other (non-host) Horrors in this book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-19T05:48:21-07:00","id":1261539,"title":"","content":"Interesting, these lamprey hosts seem to have quite a role then","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-19T22:06:46-07:00","id":1261722,"title":"","content":"And I think we're getting four more hosts? They're definitely an intriguing baddie. If it wasn't for the Hunters in Darkness and idigam I'd think they make a nice out of context antagonist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-19T22:10:26-07:00","id":1261723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1131020-night-horrors-shunned-by-the-moon?p=1261722#post1261722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I think we're getting four more hosts? They're definitely an intriguing baddie. If it wasn't for the Hunters in Darkness and idigam I'd think they make a nice out of context antagonist.</div> </div> </div> </div>I haven't had a chance to do it yet, but I think they could work well as outside context villains for 