":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-24T11:55:46-08:00","id":1276507,"title":"","content":"Looks like things are picking up pace, though there are holidays.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-01T09:34:50-08:00","id":1277847,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/bale-hounds-shunned-by-the-moon/\" target=\"_blank\">And we have a Bale Hounds preview to begin the year.</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-01T09:57:32-08:00","id":1277849,"title":"","content":"Interesting. I hope the Dark Power is expanded on at some point, it doesn't seem to do much in the spoiler, which is likely an abbreviated part of the section. Some examples for Channel Darkness would be cool but it looks sort of like the 'slight altering' you get from Gift-altering fetishes, except with a malevolent edge.<br /> <br /> I like that it takes two renown. Wonder if we're going to get some example Maeljin to help that along.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-01T10:05:57-08:00","id":1277851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1131020-night-horrors-shunned-by-the-moon?p=1277847#post1277847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/bale-hounds-shunned-by-the-moon/\" target=\"_blank\">And we have a Bale Hounds preview to begin the year.</a></div> </div> </div> </div>And I'm... scared, a bit. Not with the content of 'demon-worshiping, corruption spreading Uratha' - it's all in the idea of Bale Hounds itself. I'm just worried that powers of Corrupted can goes a bit... too much free to interpretation. Like <b>Channel Darkness:</b><br /> <br /> '<b>Channel Darkness:</b> The Bale Hound may flavor her powers with her master\u2019s domain. When using a Gift or other power that uses her chosen Renown, the <i>Asah Gadar</i> may double the Essence cost and channel the Maeljin. The player and Storyteller decide how this manifests. An attacking power may become more gruesomely effective through the influence of <i>Igsh\u2019ma</i>, or weak-minded may blurt out embarrassing secrets when confronted by <i>Bhal\u2019ma</i>\u2019s influence. At minimum, using any power this way infests the area surrounding the Bale Hound with Resonance pleasing to the Maeljin for the remainder of the scene.'<br /> <br /> It basically says 'invent your special power every time'. And this can lead to abuse of rules...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 01-01-2019, 01:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-01T10:52:18-08:00","id":1277861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1131020-night-horrors-shunned-by-the-moon?p=1277849#post1277849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting. I hope the Dark Power is expanded on at some point, it doesn't seem to do much in the spoiler, which is likely an abbreviated part of the section. Some examples for Channel Darkness would be cool but it looks sort of like the 'slight altering' you get from Gift-altering fetishes, except with a malevolent edge.<br /> <br /> I like that it takes two renown. Wonder if we're going to get some example Maeljin to help that along.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dark Power is fully written up earlier in the chapter. This excerpt refers to that part. <br /> <br /> And yes, you do get Maeljin. \ud83d\ude42","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-01T11:10:58-08:00","id":1277865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1131020-night-horrors-shunned-by-the-moon?p=1277861#post1277861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Dark Power is fully written up earlier in the chapter. This excerpt refers to that part.<br /> <br /> And yes, you do get Maeljin. \ud83d\ude42</div> </div> </div> </div>Would you mind telling me mor3 about the Igsh'ma Maeljin,the name sounds cool!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-01T11:25:02-08:00","id":1277871,"title":"","content":"will the Bale Hounds still think of The Pure as doing their job for them (making a giant wound) or see them as a legitimate threat<br /> <br /> EDIT: being a night horrors book, I won't be disappointed if the book does not go into that","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-01T11:37:41-08:00","id":1277876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1131020-night-horrors-shunned-by-the-moon?p=1277871#post1277871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">will the Bale Hounds still think of The Pure as doing their job for them (making a giant wound) or see them as a legitimate threat<br /> <br /> EDIT: being a night horrors book, I won't be disappointed if the book does not go into that</div> </div> </div> </div>We don\u2019t go into that level of detail - as you say, it\u2019s a Night Horrors book that Acro and I were allowed to run a bit free with. 2e Bale Hounds are just as happy to infiltrate Pure, which is a change from 1e where they mostly ignored them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-01T11:38:57-08:00","id":1277877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1131020-night-horrors-shunned-by-the-moon?p=1277865#post1277865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would you mind telling me mor3 about the Igsh'ma Maeljin,the name sounds cool!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That I can\u2019t do yet. \ud83d\ude09<br /> <br /> With this teaser, does it mean we now have the names of three new Maeljin, or only two?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-01T11:52:31-08:00","id":1277885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1131020-night-horrors-shunned-by-the-moon?p=1277877#post1277877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> That I can\u2019t do yet. \ud83d\ude09<br /> <br /> With this teaser, does it mean we now have the names of three new Maeljin, or only two?</div> </div> </div> </div>We have Three <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Igsh'ma<br /> Bhal'ma<br /> Lakh'ma","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-01T12:04:08-08:00","id":1277887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1131020-night-horrors-shunned-by-the-moon?p=1277876#post1277876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> We don\u2019t go into that level of detail - as you say, it\u2019s a Night Horrors book that Acro and I were allowed to run a bit free with. 2e Bale Hounds are just as happy to infiltrate Pure, which is a change from 1e where they mostly ignored them.</div> </div> </div> </div>ah ok, so not complete indifference. Thanks!<br /> <br /> EDIT: Are Bale hounds/majlin considered an equal or greater threat than Idigram?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24173,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","user":"Primordial newcomer","date":". 01-01-2019, 03:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-01T12:17:25-08:00","id":1277889,"title":"","content":"That's probably a distinction for individuals to make. Idigam are rare but pretty easily reach the level of world-ending threat. If you simplify them, Bale Hounds are twisted werewolves, and as dangerous as Pure or Ghost Wolves or heretical and charismatic Uratha.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-01T12:19:34-08:00","id":1277893,"title":"","content":"In character, Bale Hounds are seen as a more insidious threat, as you never really know if one is lurking nearby. And Bale Hounds are adept at sowing seeds of mistrust and paranoia.<br /> <br /> Plus, idigam are written as still largely unknown by the wider Uratha community. Some packs/protectorates have encountered them, most still don\u2019t know precisely what they faced, and no one is really comparing notes at this stage. Plus Uratha deal with enough weird shit that they don\u2019t necessarily know that an idigam wasn\u2019t just a really tough, strange spirit. Or something else.<br /> <br /> Out of character, personally I consider a well-run idigam to be a huge threat, with layers of minions and rabbit holes that the Uratha run down and destroy, only to later discover that there\u2019s more to do. IMO, no idigam should be a \u2018monster of the week\u2019 (though its minions could be). They should be chronicle-spanning villains who are only defeated with cunning and careful planning or dramatic sacrifice in the closing stages of the chronicle.<br /> <br /> Bale Hounds can similarly be a chronicle-wide threat, but in a different way to idigam. How can I put this... idigam can cover much of the same themes Bale Hounds can as threats, while Bale Hounds can\u2019t cover everything an idigam can.<br /> <br /> But that\u2019s just IMO.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-01T12:26:47-08:00","id":1277895,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1131020-night-horrors-shunned-by-the-moon?p=1277851#post1277851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And I'm... scared, a bit. Not with the content of 'demon-worshiping, corruption spreading Uratha' - it's all in the idea of Bale Hounds itself. I'm just worried that powers of Corrupted can goes a bit... too much free to interpretation. Like <b>Channel Darkness:</b><br /> <br /> '<b>Channel Darkness:</b> The Bale Hound may flavor her powers with her master\u2019s domain. When using a Gift or other power that uses her chosen Renown, the <i>Asah Gadar</i> may double the Essence cost and channel the Maeljin. The player and Storyteller decide how this manifests. An attacking power may become more gruesomely effective through the influence of <i>Igsh\u2019ma</i>, or weak-minded may blurt out embarrassing secrets when confronted by <i>Bhal\u2019ma</i>\u2019s influence. At minimum, using any power this way infests the area surrounding the Bale Hound with Resonance pleasing to the Maeljin for the remainder of the scene.'<br /> <br /> It basically says 'invent your special power every time'. And this can lead to abuse of rules...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Given how the player of a truly corrupt Bale Hound is likely the Storyteller or soon will be in most games, I am pretty sanguine about the abuse potential; they're horror movie villains where the protagonists are regenerating wolf demigods. Abuse is the fault of a bad ST, not a munchkin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-01T14:41:33-08:00","id":1277929,"title":"","content":"So am I the only one who looks at that preview and thinks &quot;wait, so in fact we don't even know if the Maeljin are even <i>real</i>, and not just some elaborate scheme Soulless Wolf use just to to make things even more confusing?&quot;<br /> <br /> Because seriously, when you can't see, hear or talk directly with your master and only through its servant, the chances are that your servant is your master- which is totally a Bale Hound thing to do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-01T14:53:48-08:00","id":1277934,"title":"","content":"Well yeah, If Bale Hounds can't make any type of contact with their &quot;masters&quot; then they're more or less working for Souless Wolf regardless of if the Maeljin exist or not.<br /> <br /> Especially with the emphasis put on Souless Wolf and his &quot;cliams&quot;. <br /> The whole thing can be one giant scheme.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24492,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24492-apex-predator","user":"Apex Predator","date":". 01-01-2019, 05:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24492-apex-predator","name":"Apex Predator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-01T15:02:02-08:00","id":1277935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1131020-night-horrors-shunned-by-the-moon?p=1277929#post1277929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So am I the only one who looks at that preview and thinks &quot;wait, so in fact we don't even know if the Maeljin are even <i>real</i>, and not just some elaborate scheme Soulless Wolf use just to to make things even more confusing?&quot;<br /> <br /> Because seriously, when you can't see, hear or talk directly with your master and only through its servant, the chances are that your servant is your master- which is totally a Bale Hound thing to do.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair that's the way things work with Luna. And, in-world, with Father Wolf. We may know he existed because of the Neolithic Dark Age, but werewolves have no proof. The game has always been big on faith, and potential subversions of it are kind of all over (are the Pure right? are Forsaken just slaves to lunes? are idigam the true source of Uratha? etc).<br /> <br /> I like the idea of Soulless Wolf being large and in charge, with his lies causing some multiple-personality issues as evil is never just one thing. I'd be surprised if there's a hard answer. Even the way the Renown thing works suggests there could be innumerable Maeljin depending on what angle you go at. An entity that works by subverting Glory might be big on bloody massacres that leave everyone aghast, or a personal charisma type like Polands Lycaon-Ur.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-01T15:25:34-08:00","id":1277941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1131020-night-horrors-shunned-by-the-moon?p=1277935#post1277935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To be fair that's the way things work with Luna. And, in-world, with Father Wolf. We may know he existed because of the Neolithic Dark Age, but werewolves have no proof. The game has always been big on faith, and potential subversions of it are kind of all over (are the Pure right? are Forsaken just slaves to lunes? are idigam the true source of Uratha? etc).</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, yeah, but there are a few differences by the fact that Soulless Wolf is actually the ones to &quot;suggest&quot; which Maeljin to give to the new Corrupted, and that unlike the way the Forsaken follow the words of a pantheon of lower moon gods (which all claim to serve one giant moon goddess, which is more or less how the Forsaken know the Shadow works), here there seems to be a single communication channel between the Lords of the Wounds and the Bale Hounds. It is much easier to make an elaborate scheme in the later case, than the former. But yeah, we still don't know if in 2e each of the Maeljin still have their own private spirit followers and messengers outside of Soulless Wolf's control.<br /> <br /> And I agree, I do like seeing Soulless Wolf having a bigger role in the Bale Hounds' operation. He was one of my favorite aspect of theirs in 1e, after all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-01T16:23:25-08:00","id":1277955,"title":"","content":"majlin do exist still, Bunyip say one question to have is are we introduced to three, or 2 new majlin","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-01T23:03:00-08:00","id":1278005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1131020-night-horrors-shunned-by-the-moon?p=1277929#post1277929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So am I the only one who looks at that preview and thinks &quot;wait, so in fact we don't even know if the Maeljin are even <i>real</i>, and not just some elaborate scheme Soulless Wolf use just to to make things even more confusing?&quot;<br /> <br /> Because seriously, when you can't see, hear or talk directly with your master and only through its servant, the chances are that your servant is your master- which is totally a Bale Hound thing to do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Have you ever talked to Luna? Wait, you just deal with Lunes? They could be making the whole thing up!<br /> <br /> ... \ud83d\ude09<br /> <br /> Edit: nofather beat me to it!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-01T23:05:42-08:00","id":1278006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1131020-night-horrors-shunned-by-the-moon?p=1277955#post1277955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">majlin do exist still, Bunyip say one question to have is are we introduced to three, or 2 new majlin</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Sorry, I don\u2019t quite understand the question. Or is it a statement?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-02T00:31:26-08:00","id":1278007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1131020-night-horrors-shunned-by-the-moon?p=1278006#post1278006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry, I don\u2019t quite understand the question. Or is it a statement?</div> </div> </div> </div>They're referring to this:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">With this teaser, does it mean we now have the names of three new Maeljin, or only two?</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-02T01:30:02-08:00","id":1278014,"title":"","content":"Thanks. Nicolas Milioni already answered that in post #383.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-02T08:00:03-08:00","id":1278068,"title":"","content":"sorry if this has been answered already before, but will there be magath and non-human spirit claimed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-02T14:22:13-08:00","id":1278156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1131020-night-horrors-shunned-by-the-moon?p=1278005#post1278005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Have you ever talked to Luna? Wait, you just deal with Lunes? They could be making the whole thing up!<br /> <br /> ... \ud83d\ude09</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Pay no attention to the lune behind the curtain, my children!&quot;<br /> <br /> Perhaps &quot;Luna&quot; is insane because Luna is a chorus of powerful stellar moon-spirits with their own distinct personalities and interests. I mean, if you were the spirit of Callisto would you really want to hang around Jupiter all the time or go to earth where the essence is?<br /> <br /> Maybe then the Firstborn are all half-siblings, too?<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-02T16:18:18-08:00","id":1278190,"title":"","content":"Most if not all Firstborn are already half-siblings, formed from Ur-Farah having dalliances with various spirits and possibly Pangaeans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-02T17:53:19-08:00","id":1278205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1131020-night-horrors-shunned-by-the-moon?p=1278068#post1278068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">sorry if this has been answered already before, but will there be magath and non-human spirit claimed?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes \ud83d\ude09","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-02T18:06:46-08:00","id":1278206,"title":"","content":"I don't care if that yes was only for one of those or both, now I'm even more excited for this book!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-13T20:53:04-08:00","id":1280606,"title":"","content":"Anyone else think it looks like the Maeljin are losing their Inferno associations in favor of this anti-Renown thing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-13T21:14:24-08:00","id":1280614,"title":"","content":"It doesn't seem that they're so confined by the Inferno, but that might be hopeful thinking. Originally they weren't associated with the Inferno, and they were introduced well before the Inferno book came out, then lumped into it. It would suck to have to wait for whatever the second edition Inferno equivalent is until we have Bale Hounds.<br /> <br /> That said, going by Inferno stuff you still had Malapraxes, one of which could just be renown.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-13T21:52:30-08:00","id":1280621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1131020-night-horrors-shunned-by-the-moon?p=1280606#post1280606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyone else think it looks like the Maeljin are losing their Inferno associations in favor of this anti-Renown thing?</div> </div> </div> </div>I know a lot of people are invested in the Infernal angle and therefore it's no real skin off my back if they maintain it-<br /> <br /> buuuuuuuuuuuuuuuut man I would like them to lose it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-13T21:57:50-08:00","id":1280623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1131020-night-horrors-shunned-by-the-moon?p=1280606#post1280606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyone else think it looks like the Maeljin are losing their Inferno associations in favor of this anti-Renown thing?</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, &quot;the Inferno associations&quot; of the Maeljin were just &quot;both things are Lower Depths entities&quot; with a side order of &quot;Werewolf 1e's most prominent angle on the Maeljin is tied to a variant on the seven deadly sins, which has obvious direct overlap with the book on one of the closest Depths in the cosmology which is tied to sin and atrocity.&quot;<br /> <br /> Bale Hounds fucking around with the virtues that werewolves' society puts spiritual weight on doesn't actually <i>contradict </i>anything about how the Inferno interacts with the Shadow through Wounds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-13T22:10:25-08:00","id":1280629,"title":"","content":"The Inferno should be dissociated from them as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/641-ben-linus","name":"Ben Linus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-13T22:19:55-08:00","id":1280630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ben Linus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1131020-night-horrors-shunned-by-the-moon?p=1280629#post1280629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Inferno should be dissociated from them as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're free to ask for the impossible, but again, &quot;demonic powers that work with spirits and werewolves to corrupt and undermine lauded qualities&quot; and &quot;demonic force that corrupts ghosts, the Astral, and the Shadow along the specific axes of sin and transgression&quot; are kind of inherently tangled up in each other by the nature of the subject matter.<br /> <br /> The Revised Storytelling System's decreased emphasis on a set list of Vices does much of the work of making Wound-backed werewolves distinct from more conventional infernalists without having to arbitrarily declare that <i>this</i> set of Great Unclean Ones that are so vaguely defined that it's not even clear if different names within the set refer to separate entities can't possibly be related to <i>that</i> dimension full of Great Unclean Ones who all advance through the hierarchy of sin-makers by tricking and extorting people into giving them more names.<br /> <br /> The alternative is making the Maeljin not be relevant to anything except through the lens of being related to Wounds, which brings us right back to square one because Wounds are specifically built around atrocious and disharmonious resonance, i.e. the kind of things that the Inferno <i>kind of has a vested interest in.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-13T22:38:17-08:00","id":1280634,"title":"","content":"I do not like this goetia meaning of Inferno. There are already several kingdoms that perform this function and could by the Maeljin in any of them and give them importance.<br /> <br /> The Inferno should be something primordial, before the universe, as the Persians treated them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/641-ben-linus","name":"Ben Linus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-13T22:40:31-08:00","id":1280635,"title":"","content":"It would even be interesting to be clear the difference between Inferno and Pandemonium.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/641-ben-linus","name":"Ben Linus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-13T23:23:37-08:00","id":1280641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ben Linus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1131020-night-horrors-shunned-by-the-moon?p=1280635#post1280635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It would even be interesting to be clear the difference between Inferno and Pandemonium.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's already clearly distinct.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-14T04:55:33-08:00","id":1280670,"title":"","content":"Yeah, pandemonium (God let's hope I'm talking about the right thing) is a place of torture and hardcore therapy. it's meant to cleanse ones soul and show them their wrongs. <br /> <br /> the inferno is something insidious. it thrives on vice and actively seeks to corrupt all it can into serving its needs (which again, can simply just be indulging in Vice)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-14T13:57:28-08:00","id":1280743,"title":"","content":"But the natives of both places are alike. One with more focus on punishing and the other on corrupting, but all are evil goetic spirits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/641-ben-linus","name":"Ben Linus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-14T14:01:30-08:00","id":1280745,"title":"","content":"The natives of Pandemonium are not Spirits. They are Supernal Beings. And they aren't evil; they don't have any morals. They are embodiments of the concepts of Mind and Space.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-14T14:26:00-08:00","id":1280755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1131020-night-horrors-shunned-by-the-moon?p=1280745#post1280745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The natives of Pandemonium are not Spirits. They are Supernal Beings. And they aren't evil; they don't have any morals. They are embodiments of the concepts of Mind and Space.</div> </div> </div> </div>exactly. have you ever read mage the awakening? honest question","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-14T14:27:34-08:00","id":1280757,"title":"","content":"The Demons of Pandemonium are less concerned with the vices and sins of humanity and are more interesting in challenging the limitations of the ego upon itself and the sense of self where the lines of being between individual and community are blurry if not completely non-existent, and are more fundamentally forces of painful self-improvement and self-ownership, excising the true self from the detrius of being that accumulates upon such over time, and are just as often portrayed as dark elves, fallen angels, riddling beasts and recursive shades(ie, 'fallen' versions of everyone else's denizens[not to be confused with the Abyssal incarnations]). It's not tied to a moral sense of these words, but neither is it vice centered.<br /> <br /> The Demons of the Inferno are primarily interested in the subsumption of self towards the end of being a endless wellspring of their incarnating vice-ideally, no being would have a self so much as just a long running addiction that the demon crafting the sinner could basically just buffet on forever and ever. THey also are less concerned with a need to reshape the world towards and around themselves so much as just ensuring that things spiral downward into oblivion. ANd also, yeah, they are entirely devoted to sin and vice, with no interest in anything outside of it and only interested in their escalation.<br /> <br /> THe Maeljin, possible spirit deity-satraps of the Wounds, fundamentally follow in the vein of the Wounds that are inflicted, in the same manner and form as any other spirit. In this way, their design is evocative of environmental adjustment and control as well as adaptation to those changes in kind-the pervading metaphor remains the same as the rest of Shadow Ecology, that being &quot;Wolves Reshaping the Rivers.&quot; While we are still waiting for how, exactly, they incarnate and how tied they are to mortal vice versus spiritual perversion, it cannot be ignored how they are still consequential beings within the dynamics of the Shadow and how that differs from the mindless oblivion of virtue that the Infernals offers.<br /> <br /> The first two have a clear demarcation from each other that is abundantly clear with just a little bit of actual reading. While we're not clear on the relationship of the Maeljin to mortal vice right now, it is also abundantly clear that they are still tied into the mechanics of the Shadow, and thus at best their Infernal associations are a resultant hybridization and at worst non-existant, with a high probability of coincidental parallel signifying nothing being at play in the final result.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 01-14-2019, 05:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-15T00:00:34-08:00","id":1280844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1131020-night-horrors-shunned-by-the-moon?p=1280606#post1280606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyone else think it looks like the Maeljin are losing their Inferno associations in favor of this anti-Renown thing?</div> </div> </div> </div>Uratha having Maeljin (or possibly faces of) who focus on them doesn\u2019t necessarily mean anything for other Maeljin (or their other faces).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-15T15:57:49-08:00","id":1280996,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1131020-night-horrors-shunned-by-the-moon?p=1280745#post1280745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The natives of Pandemonium are not Spirits. They are Supernal Beings. And they aren't evil; they don't have any morals. They are embodiments of the concepts of Mind and Space.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This is basically the same thing as a goetic spirit. It just does not have the same meaning as a werewolf spirit. And no problem, the supernal beings and the spirit of the shadow have to be that way, beings with mechanical mentality, essentialist (they are malignant yes, since this is a human definition) attached to the function as a cog.<br /> <br /> This does not match with any description of demons in the traditions that use them (and I am not talking about Christian demons), such as the Buddhist, Mayan, &quot;pagan&quot; and Persian tradition, that we have beings fully aware of their deeds and with discretion to decide, that even the monster of smoke has more than the beings of hell.<br /> <br /> But a metaphysical problem, Inferno functions as the deep zone of the Shadow and not as something proper.<br /> <br /> If it is to follow this line at least it states that Inferno was a zone somehow connected to Shadow. And that the Inferno was something that is where the Deviled Gods of their purposes (Mayan mythology, like the beings of the Xibalba who have become ambitious and hungry too) the primordial Shadows God (Persian mythology), Divine incarnations with a karma (Hindu, Taoist, and Buddhist mythology), and fallen or contaminated gods, angels and spirits (Christianity and paganism) and humans who have accumulated a terrible moral karma although a great intellectual level (the Dragons of Brazilian Spiritism) and as real beings and not mere reflexes that have come to fruition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/641-ben-linus","name":"Ben Linus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-15T17:11:40-08:00","id":1281011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ben Linus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1131020-night-horrors-shunned-by-the-moon?p=1280996#post1280996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> This is basically the same thing as a goetic spirit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Read: &quot;I'm not going to deal with this conversation in good faith and proper canonical context&quot;, got it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-15T17:40:20-08:00","id":1281012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ben Linus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1131020-night-horrors-shunned-by-the-moon?p=1280743#post1280743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[..] but all are evil goetic spirits.</div> </div> </div> </div>You seem to have a few misconceptions since you've mixed various game terms, but instead of being an ass about it I'll just explain them.<br /> The Shadow contains spirits, a type of ephemeral entity.<br /> The Astral contains Goetia (formerly known as goetic demons), a different type of ephemeral entity from spirits.<br /> Pandemonium contains Imps and Wraiths, collectively known as Demons, and they are Supernal entities instead of ephemeral entities. They're neither goetic nor spirits.<br /> <br /> If you actually intended the RL meanings of the words goetic and spirit, well, not a good idea when they're also well defined game terms. Ignoring the context of the conversation (in this case that you're posting in the CofD portion of the forum) is just courting unnecessary misunderstandings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-15T23:01:42-08:00","id":1281045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1131020-night-horrors-shunned-by-the-moon?p=1278005#post1278005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Have you ever talked to Luna? Wait, you just deal with Lunes? They could be making the whole thing up!<br /> <br /> ... \ud83d\ude09<br /> <br /> Edit: nofather beat me to it!</div> </div> </div> </div>Well I mean Cahalith, and potentially all Uratha who still bear a connection to Luna, receive omens and dreams from Her. So it\u2019s more like they get talked at by a vague as hell Goddess, but there is at least a symbolic form of communion that doesn\u2019t totally rely on Lunes.<br /> <br /> But The Warden Moon is nuttier than squirrel poop, so Soulless Wolf can say whatever it wants and be just as truthful as any Lune or Firstborn servitor can/ wants to be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1686,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","user":"Korogra","date":". 01-16-2019, 02:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-15T23:02:19-08:00","id":1281046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ben Linus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1131020-night-horrors-shunned-by-the-moon?p=1280996#post1280996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is basically the same thing as a goetic spirit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry Ben Linus, but right here you\u2019re just trying to shift goalposts and bring real world definitions into a debate that you helped define as game world related. Various people have rather politely pointed out the facts of where your game-related argument is wrong. Your current maneuver implies that you\u2019re aware of it as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-15T23:04:45-08:00","id":1281047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1131020-night-horrors-shunned-by-the-moon?p=1281045#post1281045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well I mean Cahalith, and potentially all Uratha who still bear a connection to Luna, receive omens and dreams from Her. So it\u2019s more like they get talked at by a vague as hell Goddess, but there is at least a symbolic form of communion that doesn\u2019t totally rely on Lunes.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, that\u2019s an assumption. Cahalith and other Uratha get omens and dreams that they take on faith as being from her. There\u2019s no independent proof this is the case. Could be powerful Rank 6+ Lunes just injecting shit into Uratha heads to perpetuate the cult.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-15T23:27:56-08:00","id":1281049,"title":"","content":"Folks like their stuff to be special.<br /> <br /> I still remember the complaints at the insinuation that the Crone of the Circle of the Crone was (gasp) a spirit, and thus 'a werewolf thing' and so made entirely worthless for vampire. I am clearly not the only one, however. In our new core book we have angels, a third party in our new ephemeral system and servants of the Mysterious God Machine who is, by definition, definitely not that thing people are thinking they might be, alongside similar things like the Principle and the Dark Mother. Then in Vampire, we have insidious strix who use ephemeral rules but NO. No they're not ephemeral, they're VAMPIRE stuff, not werewolf or mage stuff. And where do they come from? Inferno? No! It's not some blue book game. They come from a unique place of their own. Firestorms, too. Ephemeral but 'uniquely Promethean ephemerals.'<br /> <br /> In Lore of the Forsaken, they are introduced like so, 'Some see them as demons. To others they are manifestations of the Old Gods. To the werewolves, they are the Maeljin. Malicious spirit lords that grow fat on the suffering that takes place in the world. These are the creatures that carry a title unknown and meaningless in the First Tongue, for none can trace the origins of the word \u201cMaeljin\u201d. That is these Incarnae\u2019s unique distinction, and the source of no small amount of worry for the Forsaken.'<br /> <br /> They live in Wounds, not the Inferno, deep within the open sores and ragged scars of the Hisil. And they're a mystery. They may be some incarnation of the Wounds themselves. Like Father Wolf in first edition, an easy guess would be 'They're just big spirits.' We were wrong about Big Daddy.<br /> <br /> Later Inferno came out and people attributed Maeljin to Inferno, though the book seems clear to warn against that, offering them as an option for a ruleset, rather than saying 'your game is now an Inferno game.' As you can see here, 'For the purposes of this book, the Maeljin and their servants are demons. Are they one perspective upon a greater Infernal order? They share many similarities with demons from other traditions, so it\u2019s a strong possibility. If there is a pervasive, universal evil power in your World of Darkness, the Maeljin are its primal guise. The Uratha know best how to confront them on the battlefield of the Shadow, but if they are greater than even the Wounds they rule, they may have resources no werewolf can imagine: avatars on other planes, Whisperers, rituals and fell dreams to infect their spirits.'<br /> <br /> I'm sure we'll like whatever we're going to get. The writers have been generously pro-werewolf. It may not fit in your headcanon but just like after the reveals of Sundered World (and hopefully the other Dark Eras, which were eye-opening in other ways), those of us who keep track of the setting have adapted and others will too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-15T23:43:46-08:00","id":1281050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1131020-night-horrors-shunned-by-the-moon?p=1281047#post1281047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, that\u2019s an assumption. Cahalith and other Uratha get omens and dreams that they take on faith as being from her. There\u2019s no independent proof this is the case. Could be powerful Rank 6+ Lunes just injecting shit into Uratha heads to perpetuate the cult.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless the storyteller decides otherwise that is <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> It could be a Lune acting on her behalf, or Rabid Wolf fucking with the Forsaken\u2019s head for lols and/or some more sinister agenda, most definitely. <br /> <br /> Buuuut it could possibly, maybe, perchance, kinda sorta, actually be Luna. I\u2019ve always been of the opinion that a Rank 6+ Spirit of anything is an Avatar of whatever entity it claims to serve, and therefore is that entity, albeit in an almost comprehensible form.<br /> <br /> But like you said, it could equally NOT be Luna at all. It\u2019s all good either way baby, it all makes for interesting plot hooks xD<br /> <br /> Soulless Wolf could Serve the Maeljin, or could be an utter liar and just be making up any nonsense to get a leg up on his more honorable siblings.. he gets what he wants in the end either way!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-15T23:50:52-08:00","id":1281051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1131020-night-horrors-shunned-by-the-moon?p=1281050#post1281050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Unless the storyteller decides otherwise that is <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>True. And I\u2019m not saying it\u2019s not Luna, I just like Uratha faith to have some faith element to it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-15T23:57:22-08:00","id":1281053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1131020-night-horrors-shunned-by-the-moon?p=1281051#post1281051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> True. And I\u2019m not saying it\u2019s not Luna, I just like Uratha faith to have some faith element to it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Faith is a great thing, it\u2019s why the Fire-Touched are my hands down favorite Tribe. The chronicles of darkness universe is just fortunate that faith often does have tangible validation to it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-16T07:32:00-08:00","id":1281090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1131020-night-horrors-shunned-by-the-moon?p=1281053#post1281053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Fortunate is a great thing, it\u2019s why the Fire-Touched are my hands down favorite Tribe. The chronicles of darkness universe is just fortunate that faith often does have tangible validation to it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>lucky is a very subjective term when that same faith can utterly spit on you, such as benedictions being able to be used by Slashers","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-16T12:27:33-08:00","id":1281155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1131020-night-horrors-shunned-by-the-moon?p=1281046#post1281046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sorry Ben Linus, but right here you\u2019re just trying to shift goalposts and bring real world definitions into a debate that you helped define as game world related. Various people have rather politely pointed out the facts of where your game-related argument is wrong. Your current maneuver implies that you\u2019re aware of it as well.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Lack of clarity is more about having linguistic resources than bad faith.<br /> <br /> I tried to be as clear as I can be and just tried to clarify my view of distortions with each post.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/641-ben-linus","name":"Ben Linus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-16T12:58:20-08:00","id":1281169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1131020-night-horrors-shunned-by-the-moon?p=1281090#post1281090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> lucky is a very subjective term when that same faith can utterly spit on you, such as benedictions being able to be used by Slashers</div> </div> </div> </div>It is the world of darkness my friend, and just like in real life, faith is sometimes used to galvanize people into doing terrible things. The fact that it confers real power in the game is just one of those things that shows that someone is benefiting a great deal from their devotion <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-16T13:01:06-08:00","id":1281170,"title":"","content":"I suppose, but when the wrong people are getting it, well... the bible did say a serial killer was forgiven and went to heaven. it has to be quite a bombshell for any malleus malaficarum hunter to witness","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-16T16:29:37-08:00","id":1281208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ben Linus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1131020-night-horrors-shunned-by-the-moon?p=1281155#post1281155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Lack of clarity is more about having linguistic resources than bad faith.<br /> <br /> I tried to be as clear as I can be and just tried to clarify my view of distortions with each post.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The point is, in this game Spirits and Supernal Beings are different things. Period. It doesn't matter if that doesn't line up with real world uses of the names spirits, goetics, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-16T17:30:42-08:00","id":1281219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1131020-night-horrors-shunned-by-the-moon?p=1281208#post1281208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The point is, in this game Spirits and Supernal Beings are different things. Period. It doesn't matter if that doesn't line up with real world uses of the names spirits, goetics, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> What I am trying to say is that they are both creatures, so many supernal beings as spirits resemble certain attributes which in our folklore of our reality are described to goetic spirits, which is the variation used to describe all the demons or nearby things that appear in the CotD except those from Descent.<br /> <br /> I would find it more interesting to have something for the other cultural variations in the Inferno (such as those of Buddhism, Mayas and Persians - which are immensely different from each other, but resemble the demons described in CotD because they have free will and are different those of the Descent because unlike the Christian Demons they are by no means fallen or failures of some elevated entity).<br /> <br /> But I'm going to stop talking about it because I've already misplaced the topic.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/641-ben-linus","name":"Ben Linus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-16T17:41:41-08:00","id":1281220,"title":"","content":"while its appreciated that you truly drop the subject, you can't just say that &quot;in OUR reality&quot;. that's not right, this is the chronicles of darkness, not OUR reality but a game of roleplaying","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-16T20:42:54-08:00","id":1281246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ben Linus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1131020-night-horrors-shunned-by-the-moon?p=1281219#post1281219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> What I am trying to say is that they are both creatures, so many supernal beings as spirits resemble certain attributes which in our folklore of our reality are described to goetic spirits, which is the variation used to describe all the demons or nearby things that appear in the CotD except those from Descent.<br /> <br /> I would find it more interesting to have something for the other cultural variations in the Inferno (such as those of Buddhism, Mayas and Persians - which are immensely different from each other, but resemble the demons described in CotD because they have free will and are different those of the Descent because unlike the Christian Demons they are by no means fallen or failures of some elevated entity).<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>If you want something resembling our reality to show up in the games then that seems like a topic to bring up with the Devs in a separate thread perhaps; trying to bring up the issue in a thread about the gameline as it currently is resolves nothing because the gameline isn't made to fit your idea of how things should be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24492-apex-predator","name":"Apex Predator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-16T23:00:53-08:00","id":1281259,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Apex Predator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1131020-night-horrors-shunned-by-the-moon?p=1281246#post1281246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you want something resembling our reality to show up in the games then that seems like a topic to bring up with the Devs in a separate thread perhaps; trying to bring up the issue in a thread about the gameline as it currently is resolves nothing because the gameline isn't made to fit your idea of how things should be.</div> </div> </div> </div>I did not think I would stagger like that and above all I could not get my idea right, so I kept trying to be clearer. In fact I should have addressed this topic in another topic and in another part of the forum. In CotD in general and not in werewolf .. Much less in Night Horrors.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1131020-night-horrors-shunned-by-the-moon?p=1281220#post1281220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">while its appreciated that you truly drop the subject, you can't just say that &quot;in OUR reality&quot;. that's not right, this is the chronicles of darkness, not OUR reality but a game of roleplaying</div> </div> </div> </div>Because I was referring to how the concept is treated in our reality, in our culture (and hence the signs it was using) to say that I believe that the subject was not being translated formally in the Chronicles (since all concepts in the game are based in elements of mythology, pop culture and common folklore treated unpredictably, but a vampire is something described outside and therefore translated with respect to his tradition in the game).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":641,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/641-ben-linus","user":"Ben Linus","date":". 01-17-2019, 02:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/641-ben-linus","name":"Ben Linus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-18T06:24:17-08:00","id":1281499,"title":"","content":"Darker Days Radio interviewed DaveB and I at Dragonmeet in December, and the recording has now gone up; among other things, we talked a little about Shunned by the Moon <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://podcast.darker-days.org/e/96-the-annual-dragonmeet-coffee-bar-special/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://d2bwo9zemjwxh5.cloudfront.net/image-logo/286887/darkerdays_sq_1200x628.jpg?s=ef9d996b77a32657cc00ba35c6884454&amp;e=jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://podcast.darker-days.org/e/96-the-annual-dragonmeet-coffee-bar-special/\" target=\"_blank\"> #97: The Annual Dragonmeet Coffee Bar Special | Darker Days Radio </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://podcast.darker-days.org/e/96-the-annual-dragonmeet-coffee-bar-special/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://podcast.darker-days.org/e/96-the-annual-dragonmeet-coffee-bar-special/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Chris was at Dragonmeet 2018, in London last December, a day after getting back from Boston, and he sat down with&nbsp;Onyx Path Publishing&nbsp;freelancers and developers&nbsp;David Brookshaw&nbsp;and&nbsp;Christopher Allen. They chat all about the releases coming up, plus some more exclusive information for&nbsp;Mummy: the Curse 2nd Edition&nbsp;and&nbsp;Deviant: the Renegades. &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Be sure to check us out on&nbsp;Facebook&nbsp;or through our Google Plus Community. To stay up to date,&nbsp;subscribe through iTunes!&nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Links For This Episode:&nbsp;&nbsp; White Wolf Entertainment: http://www.white-wolf.com/ Occam's Laser Music: https://occamslaser.bandcamp.com/ Midnight Express Podcast: https://midnightexpress.podbean.com/ Mike's History Podcast on the Satanic Panic: http://historylessons.libsyn.com/161-the-satanic-panic Full Metal RPG Podcast: http://fullmetalrpg.com/ &nbsp; </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":1757,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","user":"Acrozatarim","date":".  Updating link 01-18-2019, 10:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-06T11:20:52-08:00","id":1285309,"title":"","content":"in the video recently posted today. Hosts toads and locusts are mentioned (though I thought locust were already panned)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data: